%% MyBook — deployment diagram (Dağıtım diyagramı)
%% Where each part runs and how the nodes talk. Web, API and database are separate nodes:
%% the browser only ever talks to the web server; the web server calls the API; only the API
%% touches the database. Ports are the ones the project uses (web 3000, API 4000, Supabase pooler 6543).
%% Mermaid has no deployment-diagram type, so nodes are frames and artifacts are boxes inside them.
flowchart LR
  subgraph Client["«device» User device"]
    Browser["«execution environment»<br/>Web browser<br/>— pages, service worker (offline pass)"]
  end

  subgraph WebNode["«node» Web server · Node.js ≥ 22"]
    NextApp["«artifact»<br/>apps/web<br/>Next.js 16 (SSR, server actions)<br/>:3000"]
  end

  subgraph ApiNode["«node» Application server · Node.js ≥ 22"]
    NestApp["«artifact»<br/>apps/api<br/>NestJS REST API + Prisma<br/>:4000 /api"]
    Jobs["«artifact»<br/>scheduled job<br/>hold expiry"]
  end

  subgraph Supabase["«node» Supabase cloud · eu-central-1"]
    Postgres[("«database»<br/>PostgreSQL<br/>via PgBouncer pooler :6543")]
    Auth["«service»<br/>Supabase Auth<br/>JWT + JWKS"]
    Bucket["«service»<br/>Storage · covers bucket<br/>public CDN"]
  end

  subgraph Providers["«node» External book APIs"]
    Google["Google Books API"]
    OpenLib["Open Library API"]
    Apple["Apple Books Search API"]
  end

  Browser -->|HTTPS · HTML, server actions| NextApp
  Browser -->|HTTPS · cover images via /_next/image| NextApp
  NextApp -->|HTTPS · REST/JSON · Bearer JWT| NestApp
  NextApp -->|HTTPS · sign-in, session cookies| Auth
  NextApp -->|HTTPS · image optimizer fetch| Bucket
  NestApp -->|TCP · SQL over TLS| Postgres
  Jobs --- NestApp
  NestApp -->|HTTPS · public keys| Auth
  NestApp -->|HTTPS · upload covers| Bucket
  NestApp -->|HTTPS · ISBN / title lookup| Google
  NestApp -->|HTTPS| OpenLib
  NestApp -->|HTTPS| Apple
